This plugin does not port or reimplement any part of the core Bank Tags tab
strip. The core plugin draws its own column and this one rearranges it. What is
derived from the core source is limited to the small amount of shared knowledge
needed to cooperate with it:

  - The condition used to detect a bank resize inside [proc,bankmain_size_check]
    (which stack arguments hold the widget, width and height), taken from
    TabInterface.onScriptPreFired.

  - The one-pixel gap between rows, and the convention that a widget's options
    are numbered from index one, both matching TabInterface so that folder rows
    line up with tag tabs and behave like them.

  - The observation that nulling the dragged-on widget is how a drop is
    cancelled, which TabInterface documents in a comment and uses to honour its
    own "prevent tag tab drags" setting.

Everything else about the core column -- its height, its width, the number of
rows that fit, where the first row starts, and the sprite behind a tab -- is
read off the widgets the core plugin has already created, at runtime, rather
than copied from its source.

